---
import CortexLegalLayout from '../../layouts/CortexLegalLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY, getApp } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('cortex')!;
const effectiveDate = 'August 21, 2026';
const policyVersion = '1.0';
const title = `${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`;
const description =
  'How Cortex handles on-device game data, private iCloud Sudoku statistics, widgets, and optional Apple Game Center services.';
---

<CortexLegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/cortex/privacy/"
  page="privacy"
  heading="Cortex Privacy Policy"
  documentMeta={`Version ${policyVersion} · Effective ${effectiveDate}`}
  summary="Cortex keeps gameplay on your iPhone. Nintek does not operate a Cortex account, analytics service, advertising service, or gameplay backend."
>
  <div class="cx-legal-layout">
    <nav class="cx-legal-toc" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <strong>On this page</strong>
      <a href="#short-version">The short version</a>
      <a href="#local-data">Data on your iPhone</a>
      <a href="#icloud">Private iCloud sync</a>
      <a href="#widgets">Widgets and App Group data</a>
      <a href="#game-center">Optional Game Center</a>
      <a href="#retention">Retention and deletion</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="cx-legal-copy">
      <section id="short-version" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p class="cx-legal-callout">
          Cortex has no custom account or login, no Nintek-operated backend or API,
          no ads, no tracking, no analytics SDK, and no current purchase,
          subscription, or payment feature. Nintek does not receive your gameplay,
          settings, scores, achievements, advertising identifier, or Apple Account
          credentials through the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cortex can use Apple services you control: private iCloud key-value
          storage for Sudoku statistics, an App Group for its own widgets, and
          optional Game Center for Apple-managed player identity, leaderboards, and
          achievements. Apple processes those services under Apple’s terms and
          privacy practices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="developer-data" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Information Nintek receives</h2>
        <p>
          The Cortex app does not send personal information or gameplay data to
          {COMPANY.name}. If you email us, we receive the address and information
          you choose to include so we can respond. Cortex does not automatically
          attach local game data, your Apple Account, or your Game Center profile
          to a support message.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="local-data" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Data stored on your iPhone</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex stores game progress, active runs, settings, play history,
          statistics, records, and pending Game Center submissions locally with
          Apple’s UserDefaults and Codable storage APIs. This data remains inside
          the app’s storage on your iPhone unless an Apple service described below
          handles a limited copy. Nintek does not receive a server copy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cortex does not request access to your location, contacts, camera,
          microphone, photo library, or notifications. It uses Apple’s haptic
          frameworks for supported gameplay feedback without requesting a
          sensitive-data permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="icloud" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Private iCloud key-value storage</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex writes Sudoku statistics, including difficulty results, streaks,
          times, and recent games, to Apple’s private iCloud key-value store when
          you are signed in to iCloud and the service is available. A local copy is
          also kept on the iPhone. This is limited Sudoku-statistics sync; Cortex
          does not claim that every game’s data or active run syncs through iCloud.
        </p>
        <p>
          Apple associates the private store with your Apple Account and controls
          its transport, availability, and retention. Nintek does not operate the
          iCloud service and cannot inspect, merge, restore, or delete data in your
          Apple Account. You can manage which apps use iCloud in Apple Settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118225">
            Apple: change which apps sync and store data with iCloud
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="widgets" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Widgets and App Group data</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex writes a compact snapshot to its private App Group so the Cortex
          Quick Launch and Stats widgets can show a selected game, total plays,
          time played, games tried, and progress toward an achievement. The App
          Group is shared only by Cortex and its own widget extension. It is not a
          Nintek server and does not transmit the snapshot to Nintek.
        </p>
        <p>
          You choose whether to add or remove a Cortex widget through Apple’s Home
          Screen interfaces. Removing a widget stops it from appearing but does not
          by itself erase Cortex’s local app data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="game-center" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Optional Apple Game Center</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex remains playable without a Cortex account and without using Game
          Center. If you use Game Center, Apple authenticates the local player and
          handles the player name, Game Center identifier, leaderboards, scores,
          achievements, and related profile activity. Cortex may keep pending
          scores and achievement progress locally until Apple’s service is
          available.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nintek does not receive your Apple Account password or operate the Game
          Center account system. Game Center records are controlled by Apple and
          may remain in your Apple Account after Cortex is deleted.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/iphone/set-up-your-game-center-profile-iphd26b2beaa/ios">
              Apple: set up and manage a Game Center profile
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://privacy.apple.com/">Apple Data and Privacy</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="tracking" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Advertising, analytics, tracking, and payments</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex contains no advertising SDK, analytics SDK, tracking SDK, or
          third-party payment SDK. It does not track you across other companies’
          apps or websites. There are currently no in-app purchases,
          subscriptions, paid upgrades, or external payment links in Cortex.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="notices" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Third-party notices and content provenance</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex ships no third-party SDKs. Its in-app <strong>Content &amp;
          Provenance</strong> screen identifies the retained ENABLE-derived
          Wordfoundry corpus and the first-party or owner-attested sources used for
          visual content, including six owner-generated GPT-Image-2 sheets. The
          canonical notices and machine-readable provenance record are bundled
          with the app and can be exported from that screen.
        </p>
        <p>
          The former OpenMoji-derived Pixel Flow content was removed and does not
          ship in the current remediation build. Content notices describe source
          and rights records; opening the games does not contact those content
          providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Retention, reset, and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Local game data remains on your iPhone until Cortex changes it or you
          delete the app. A game’s restart or reset control starts a new board or
          run; it is not an erase-all privacy control. Cortex currently has no
          single in-app control that removes every local preference, statistic,
          saved run, and widget snapshot.
        </p>
        <p>
          Deleting Cortex removes its on-device app and App Group data from that
          iPhone. It does not delete your Apple Account, Game Center profile,
          leaderboards, achievements, or Apple-held iCloud data. If private iCloud
          Sudoku statistics remain available, they may return after reinstalling
          Cortex. Use Apple’s iCloud and Game Center controls for Apple-held data;
          Nintek cannot perform that deletion for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Support correspondence may be retained as needed to answer the request,
          document the issue, meet legal obligations, or protect the service. You
          may ask us to delete support correspondence, subject to applicable legal
          or security requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children-regions" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Children and regional privacy rights</h2>
        <p>
          Cortex is a general-audience game collection. It does not knowingly send
          a child’s personal information or gameplay to a Nintek service. Apple’s
          age, family, consent, and account controls apply when a child uses iCloud
          or Game Center.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy laws in your region may provide rights over personal information
          a business holds. Nintek does not hold Cortex gameplay or Apple-service
          account data. If you believe we hold personal information in support
          correspondence, contact us so we can review the request. Requests about
          an Apple Account, iCloud, or Game Center must be directed to Apple.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy if Cortex, Apple service integrations, or our
          data practices change. The version and effective date at the top identify
          the policy currently published for Cortex.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="cx-legal-section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or information you sent to Nintek? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
          For help using Cortex, visit <a href="/cortex/support/">Cortex Support</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</CortexLegalLayout>
